S = {
1: "Long after the rockets disappeared into the sky, something remained. Across the silent landscapes of the Moon and Mars, machines, instruments, and fragments of human exploration still stand. They are reminders of journeys that changed our understanding of the universe.",
2: "In 1969, Apollo 11 brought humanity to the Moon. But when the astronauts returned home, they did not bring everything back. The descent stages of lunar modules, scientific instruments, cameras, and other equipment were left behind. Each object had a purpose. Each became part of the history of lunar exploration.",
3: "Later Apollo missions left even more behind. The Lunar Roving Vehicle carried astronauts across the lunar surface. Scientific experiment packages studied the Moon. Retroreflectors still help scientists measure the distance between Earth and the Moon. Some of these forgotten machines continue to serve science today.",
4: "Then came Mars. In 1976, the Viking landers reached the Red Planet. Pathfinder and its tiny companion, Sojourner, followed decades later. Spirit, Opportunity, Curiosity, and Perseverance carried our search for knowledge even further. These robotic explorers transformed distant landscapes into places we could study.",
5: "But why were these machines left behind? Some were designed to remain after their missions ended. Others stopped working because of damaged systems, harsh environments, depleted power, or lost communication. The Moon and Mars preserve the physical traces of both successful missions and unexpected endings.",
6: "From lunar landing stages to silent Martian rovers, every piece of hardware tells a story. Some still provide scientific value. Others survive through photographs, orbital observations, and mission records. What once represented the cutting edge of engineering has become a historical footprint of humanity beyond Earth.",
7: "New missions will continue exploring these worlds. New machines will arrive, and new discoveries will be made. But the explorers who came before will never truly disappear. Their missions may have ended. Their legacy remains.",
}
